cture, kernel state-threading, demand, and budget backstop — EXCEPT for one missed P1 completeness defect (`::hits` key collision across concurrent leader activations; see Question 4, D1).**\n\n- **Single kernel, lexical scope vs. invocation progress, constant stack**:\n  - [`emit-rule`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2086-L2110), [`rule-fixpoint`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2057-L2083), [`rule-iteration`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2011-L2055), and [`read-table`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L1995-L2008) run on the shared `[state result]` trampoline (`bounce` / `bind` / `each-st`) with zero atoms, volatiles, or dynamic vars.\n  - `::tables` is scoped lexically to `body-ctx` ([query.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2016)), leaving caller `ctx` untouched on return while threading `st` forward across passes, definitions, and sibling branches — honoring the r3 ruling ([1792862294000-architect-datomic-q-phase4-stop-r3.gpt-6-astra.findings.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/archive/dao-space-query/1792862294000-architect-datomic-q-phase4-stop-r3.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L54-L63)).\n  - Call keys `[rule-name (binding-key arg-vals)]` and tuple deduplication `(binding-key tuple)` preserve CBOR content-strict numeric identity (`1` vs. `1.0`, `1.0M` vs. `1.00M`, `+0.0` vs. `-0.0`), and `:seen` / `:new` update before [`unify-call`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2047-L2048) so repeated call-site variables like `(path ?x ?x)` retain off-diagonal intermediate tuples in the table across passes.\n  - First-witness existential demand (`not` / `not-join` via [`exists-st`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L1878-L1885)) short-circuits mid-pass through `reduced`, and every pass that re-enters a table charges at least `:rule-entry` (plus `:candidate` per tabled tuple), guaranteeing structured `:step-budget-exhausted` termination on fresh-value divergence.\n- **Why single-call left/right/both/mutual recursion converges (Bekić's theorem), and where multi-call conjunctions break (D1)**:\n  - For a single top-level call, nested different-key leaders compute $\\mu T_{K'}.\\,F_{K'}(T_{\\text{anc}} \\cup \\{K \\mapsto T_K\\}, T_{K'})$ monotonically per outer pass, reaching the joint least fixed point by Bekić's theorem.\n  - **However**, because [`rule-iteration`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2049) streams each newly discovered tuple to the caller continuation `k` *before* the outer pass finishes, `k` executes under the caller's `ctx` (where `call-key` is absent from `::tables`). Whenever `k` evaluates a second call with the **same `call-key`** (for example, `[:find ?x ?y :in $ % :where (path 1 ?x) (path 1 ?y)]` with `left-rules`), the inner [`rule-fixpoint`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2068-L2082) clears `call-key` from the shared `(::hits st)` set, prematurely terminating the outer fixed-point loop and **dropping valid answers** (full trace in **Question 4, D1**).\n\n---\n\n## 2. Vector-Head Stratification Fix (Review P1)\n\n**Closes the vector-head vs. list-head bypass as specified, with one residual malformed-head edge case (Question 4, D3).**\n\n- Changing `(seq? (first %))` to `(sequential? (first %))` in [`check-rules-stratified!`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2552) brings both `[(p ?x) ...]` and `[[p ?x] ...]` (including required-bound `[[p [?x] ?y] ...]`) under the pre-evaluation cycle check in [`q-with-state`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2703-L2704) with zero source reads.\n- [`collect-rule-calls`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2524-L2543) accurately mirrors [`emit-clause`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2112-L2127) across `not`, `not-join`, `and`, `or`, and `or-join`, and `reach` follows both positive and negated edges from every negated callee, catching self-negation and arbitrary multi-hop cycles through negation while admitting stratified negation outside the cycle.\n- **Residual gap (D3)**: Because neither [`rule-head`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L1953-L1966) nor [`emit-rule`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2093) requires `(sequential? head)`, a non-sequential collection head such as a set `'[[#{p} [1 :e 2] (not (p))]]` still skips `(sequential? (first %))` in `check-rules-stratified!` while evaluating in `emit-rule`/`rule-head` (see **D3**).\n\n---\n\n## 3. E15/E16 Convention Freezes, `cell-same?` Bijection, and Corpus Graduation\n\n**Meets the freeze-via-fixtures discipline, EXCEPT for a factual error in E16's adapter-category description (Question 4, D4).**\n\n- **Corpus and provenance integrity**: Verified all `113` cases (`56` executable, `9` difference, `19` refusal, `29` pending), `28` points, and `12` fixtures across [datomic-q-v1.json](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/test/resources/dao/space/datomic-q-v1.json), [datomic-q-v1.provenance.edn](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/test/resources/dao/space/datomic-q-v1.provenance.edn#L9-L13), [datomic-q-v1.README.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/test/resources/dao/space/datomic-q-v1.README.md#L129-L130), and [`resource-blake3`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/test/dao/space/datomic_query_conformance_test.cljc#L95-L100) (`51e021815d94ea0f9e4a9af119590c19af2a7450b20db7c7e918c0a0c7bb128c`). All 14 `rules.*` cases and `agg.non-variable-argument` honestly record `\"evidence\": \"local-dao-source\"` and `\"oracle\": \"pending\"`.\n- **Phase 2 carries resolved cleanly**:\n  - [`cell-same?`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/test/dao/space/datomic_query_conformance_test.cljc#L322-L332) now enforces a consuming one-to-one matching (exact because numeric-value equality `(zero? (cbor/num-compare a b))` is an equivalence relation on numerics).\n  - [`parse-aggregate`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2374-L2376) (backed by [`check-declared-symbols`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2477-L2481) for bare/`_` symbols) refuses non-variable aggregate arguments statically, and [`validate-clauses!`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2192-L2194) + [`clause-bound-vars`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2501) refuse non-flat rule calls cleanly.\n  - E15 ([datomic-q-v1.errata.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/test/resources/dao/space/datomic-q-v1.errata.md#L242-L251)) accurately records the two-layer `rand`/`sample` refusal, `(max n ?x)` tie order, and the non-variable aggregate-arg refusal.\n- **Inaccuracy in E16 (D4)**: E16 ([datomic-q-v1.errata.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datom