     Both clauses share `call-key = ['path (binding-key [1 FREE])]`. During Pass 1 of outer `(path 1 ?x)`, Def 1 calls [`read-table`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2001) once before `each-st` (setting `::hits = #{K}`), derives `[1 3]` (`?x = 3`), and streams to `k` (`(path 1 ?y)`). Inner `(path 1 ?y)` sees `table = nil` in outer `ctx`, runs its own `rule-fixpoint` for `K`, and exits at [line 2082](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2082) via `:else [(clear-hit st K) acc']` — **erasing `K` from `(::hits st)`**. Outer Pass 1 finishes with `(:new a2) = [[1 3]]` and `(hit? st K) => false`, stopping at Pass 1 and silently losing `?x = 1` and `?x = 4` (returning 8 of 16 rows; with recursive-first definition order, stopping at Pass 0 and losing `?x = 3` as well). The same bug hits `(path ?a ?b) (path ?c ?d)` (`K = ['path [FREE FREE]]`) and `(path 1 ?x) (not-join [?x] (path 1 ?z) ...)`. Conversely, [line 2078](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2078) (`stopped? [st (reduced acc')]`) omits `clear-hit`, leaking an inner `exists-st` hit into `st`.\n   - **Why existing tests missed it**: [`a-rule-used-twice-in-one-query-is-independent-per-call`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/test/dao/space/query_rules_test.cljc#L163-L166) used `(path 1 ?x) (path 5 ?y)` (distinct keys), and [`execution_test.cljc:426`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/dao/space/query/execution_test.cljc#L426) used right-recursive `chain-rules` (which binds `?m` to distinct keys and never needs Pass 1).\n   - **Recommended correction**: Capture `was-hit? (hit? st call-key)` on entry to [`rule-fixpoint`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2066) and restore `(if was-hit? (note-hit st call-key) (clear-hit st call-key))` on both `stopped?` ([line 2078](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2078)) and `:else` ([line 2082](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2082)), leaving `(exec/terminal? st)` untouched (or allocate a unique table-activation ID in `st`). Pin same-key sibling calls `(path 1 ?x) (path 1 ?y)` with `left-rules` (both clause orders) and `(path 1 ?x) (not-join [?x] (path 1 ?z) ...)` in [query_rules_test.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/test/dao/space/query_rules_test.cljc).\n\n2. **P2 (Gate Blocker) | [jolt_j2_lane.clj:253-274](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj#L253-L274) | `dao.space.query-rules-test` is unlisted in the Jolt J2 manifest (D2)**\n   - **Evidence**: Branch `datomic-q-p3-ci` adds portable [query_rules_test.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/test/dao/space/query_rules_test.cljc) without adding `\"dao.space.query-rules-test\"` to `included` in [jolt_j2_lane.clj](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj). Merging as-is will break [`check-manifest!`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj#L327-L363) on `master` (`J2 manifest FAILED: UNLISTED dao.space.query-rules-test`, sixth recurrence) and omit a pure query suite required by [dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md:924-925](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/docs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md#L924-L925).\n   - **Recommended correction**: Add `\"dao.space.query-rules-test\"` to `included` in [jolt_j2_lane.clj](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj#L256) and run the Jolt single-namespace check before merge.\n\n3. **P2 | [query.cljc:1958-1966, 2093, 2552](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L1958-L1966) | Non-sequential rule heads bypass `check-rules-stratified!` or misclassify as `:evaluation-failed` (D3)**\n   - **Evidence**: [`check-rules-stratified!`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2552) filters by `(sequential? (first %))`, whereas [`emit-rule`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2093) uses `(first (first %))` and [`rule-head`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L1959) uses `(vec (rest head))`. A set head `'[[#{p} [1 :e 2] (not (p))]]` skips `check-rules-stratified!` (`(sequential? #{p}) => false`) yet evaluates in `emit-rule`/`rule-head` without refusal; a scalar head `'[[123 [1 :e 2]]]` throws raw host `IllegalArgumentException` in `(first (first %))`, surfacing at the adapter as `:evaluation-failed` (`fault`) instead of `:invalid-request` (`incorrect`).\n   - **Recommended correction**: Require `(and (sequential? rule) (sequential? (first rule)) (symbol? (ffirst rule)))` in rule validation / [`rule-head`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L1958) (throwing `ex-info` `\"malformed rule head\"` with `{:head ...}`) so stratification, core evaluation, and adapter `:invalid-request` classification share one exact head grammar.\n\n4. **P2 | [datomic-q-v1.errata.md:117-119](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/test/resources/dao/space/datomic-q-v1.errata.md#L117-L119) | E16 misstates the adapter error discriminator for unbound required-bound rule calls (D4)**\n   - **Evidence**: Core throws `(ex-info \"Rule required-bound variable is not bound at the call\" {:rule rule-name, :var ...})` ([query.cljc:2026-2027](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2026-L2027)). Because `(some? (ex-data e))` is true, [`classify-core-failure`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query/datomic.cljc#L579-L583) maps it to **`:invalid-request`** (`:cognitect.anomalies/incorrect`), pinned at [query_rules_test.cljc:375-377](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/test/dao/space/query_rules_test.cljc#L375-L377) — not `:evaluation-failed` (`:cognitect.anomalies/fault`).\n   - **Recommended correction**: Update E16 to name `:invalid-request` (`:cognitect.anomalies/incorrect`, via the adapter's generic core-`ex-info` refusal path, consistent with unbound fn/`not-join` variables), keeping Datomic's exact category on the Phase 5 oracle measurement list.\n\n5. **P3 | [dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md:233](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/docs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md#L233) | Stale `active-call guard` text in adjacent supported-domain row (D5)**\n   - **Recommended correction**: While editing the branch for D1–D4, update row 233 (`Finite positive recursive rules`) alongside row 232 so it no longer states `\"Current active-call guard is not a completeness proof\"`.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Sign-Off Verdict\n\nNOT SIGNED OFF: Fix D1 (`rule-fixpoint` `::hits` preservation across nested same-`call-key` leader activations on both normal and `reduced` exits, with left-recursive same-key conjunction/negation regression tests), D2 (register `\"dao.space.query-rules-test\"` in `src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj` and verify on Jolt), D3 (reject non-sequential/malformed rule heads uniformly with `ex-info` so stratification cannot be bypassed by set heads and adapter errors stay `:invalid-request`), and D4 (correct `:evaluation-failed` to `:invalid-request` in `datomic-q-v1.errata.md` E16; optionally fold D5 on `dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md:233`), then re-verify and return for confirmation and 