and the two stream-engineer review findings ([1792962000000-stream-engineer-datomic-q-phase3-review.glm-5.3.findings.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792962000000-stream-engineer-datomic-q-phase3-review.glm-5.3.findings.md) and [1792962000000-stream-engineer-datomic-q-phase3-confirm.glm-5.3.findings.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792962000000-stream-engineer-datomic-q-phase3-confirm.glm-5.3.findings.md)). A few `collab/` filenames had slightly different paths or extensions, so I will locate the exact `collab/` files, read the remainder of [dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md) and [orchestrator.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/agents/roles/orchestrator.md), and inspect the `master..datomic-q-p3-ci` diff.\\nLocating the archived Phase 2 sign-off prompt, reading the QA engineer Phase 3 logs (`.stdout.log`), and checking [architect.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/agents/roles/architect.md) and [delegate-invocation-reference.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/agents/delegate-invocation-reference.md) for the exact architect sign-off protocol.\\nReading the archived Phase 2 architect sign-off prompt and findings ([1792962000000-architect-datomic-q-phase2-signoff.prompt.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/archive/dao-space-query/1792962000000-architect-datomic-q-phase2-signoff.prompt.md) and [1792962000000-architect-datomic-q-phase2-signoff.gemini-4-argon.findings.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/archive/dao-space-query/1792962000000-architect-datomic-q-phase2-signoff.gemini-4-argon.findings.md)), along with the full `git diff master..datomic-q-p3-ci`.\\nCompleted-GMT: 2026-10-26 14:29:02 GMT\\nCompleted-Local: 2026-10-26 21:29:02 +07\\nCoding-Agent: agy\\nSession-ID: 19a3d247-adc0-4f98-9d2b-e03cd1c5f3f5\\n\\n# Lead System Architect Sign-Off Review — `dao.space.query.datomic` Phase 3 (`164da9c0f`)\\n\\n**Reviewed Range**: `master...datomic-q-p3-ci` (`8f31f8f23..164da9c0f`, 10 files changed, `+699/-67`; disjoint from `8f31f8f23..master` at `671cd21f4`).\\n**Method**: Read-only static and mathematical audit of the full diff, evaluator kernel, adapter boundary, errata, conformance corpus (`113` cases: `56` executable, `9` difference, `19` refusal, `29` pending; `28` points; `12` fixtures verified via Python JSON inspection), and the Jolt J2 applicability manifest ([jolt_j2_lane.clj](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj)). (Host JVM/Chez execution under `~/.local` is blocked in headless `--mode plan --sandbox`, per [delegate-invocation-reference.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/agents/delegate-invocation-reference.md#L280-L292); jupiter three-host and downstream gates are evaluated as orchestrator/reviewer evidence.)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Tabling Fixed-Point Completeness vs. r3-Era Kernel Requirements\\n\\n**Sound in core Bekić fixed-point structure, kernel state-threading, demand, and budget backstop — EXCEPT for one missed P1 completeness defect (`::hits` key collision across concurrent leader activations; see Question 4, D1).**\\n\\n- **Single kernel, lexical scope vs. invocation progress, constant stack**:\\n  - [`emit-rule`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2086-L2110), [`rule-fixpoint`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2057-L2083), [`rule-iteration`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2011-L2055), and [`read-table`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L1995-L2008) run on the shared `[state result]` trampoline (`bounce` / `bind` / `each-st`) with zero atoms, volatiles, or dynamic vars.\\n  - `::tables` is scoped lexically to `body-ctx` ([query.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2016)), leaving caller `ctx` untouched on return while threading `st` forward across passes, definitions, and sibling branches — honoring the r3 ruling ([1792862294000-architect-datomic-q-phase4-stop-r3.gpt-6-astra.findings.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/archive/dao-space-query/1792862294000-architect-datomic-q-phase4-stop-r3.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L54-L63)).\\n  - Call keys `[rule-name (binding-key arg-vals)]` and tuple deduplication `(binding-key tuple)` preserve CBOR content-strict numeric identity (`1` vs. `1.0`, `1.0M` vs. `1.00M`, `+0.0` vs. `-0.0`), and `:seen` / `:new` update before [`unify-call`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2047-L2048) so repeated call-site variables like `(path ?x ?x)` retain off-diagonal intermediate tuples in the table across passes.\\n  - First-witness existential demand (`not` / `not-join` via [`exists-st`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L1878-L1885)) short-circuits mid-pass through `reduced`, and every pass that re-enters a table charges at least `:rule-entry` (plus `:candidate` per tabled tuple), guaranteeing structured `:step-budget-exhausted` termination on fresh-value divergence.\\n- **Why single-call left/right/both/mutual recursion converges (Bekić's theorem), and where multi-call conjunctions break (D1)**:\\n  - For a single top-level call, nested different-key leaders compute $\\\\mu T_{K'}.\\\\,F_{K'}(T_{\\\\text{anc}} \\\\cup \\\\{K \\\\mapsto T_K\\\\}, T_{K'})$ monotonically per outer pass, reaching the joint least fixed point by Bekić's theorem.\\n  - **However**, because [`rule-iteration`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2049) streams each newly discovered tuple to the caller continuation `k` *before* the outer pass finishes, `k` executes under the caller's `ctx` (where `call-key` is absent from `::tables`). Whenever `k` evaluates a second call with the **same `call-key`** (for example, `[:find ?x ?y :in $ % :where (path 1 ?x) (path 1 ?y)]` with `left-rules`), the inner [`rule-fixpoint`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2068-L2082) clears `call-key` from the shared `(::hits st)` set, prematurely terminating the outer fixed-point loop and **dropping valid answers** (full trace in **Question 4, D1**).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Vector-Head Stratification Fix (Review P1)\\n\\n**Closes the vector-head vs. list-head bypass as specified, with one residual malformed-head edge case (Question 4, D3).**\\n\\n- Changing `(seq? (first %))` to `(sequential? (first %))` in [`check-rules-stratified!`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2552) brings both `[(p ?x) ...]` and `[[p ?x] ...]` (including required-bound `[[p [?x] ?y] ...]`) under the pre-evaluation cycle check in [`q-with-state`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2703-L2704) with zero source reads.\\n- [`collect-rule-calls`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2524-L2543) accurately mirrors [`emit-clause`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2112-L2127) across `not`, `not-join`, `and`, `or`, and `or-join`, and `reach` follows both positive and negated edges from every negated callee, catching self-negation and arbitrary multi-hop cycles through negation while admitting stratified negation outside the cycle.\\n- **Residual gap (D3)**: Because neither [`rule-head`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L1953-L1966) nor [`emit-rule`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2093) requires `(sequential? head)`, a non-sequential collection head such as a set `'[[#{p} [1 :e 2] (not (p))]]` still skips `(sequential? (first %))` in `check-rules-stratified!` while evaluating in `emit-rule`/`rule-head` (see **D3**).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. E15/E16 Convention Freezes, `cell-same?` Bijection, and Corpus Graduation\\n\\n**Meets the freeze-via-fixtures discipline, EXCEPT for a factual error in E16's adapter-category description (Question 4, D4).**\\n\\n- **Corpus and provenance integrity**: Verified all `113` cases (`56` executable, `9` difference, `19` refusal, `29` pending), `28` points, and `12` fixtures across [datomic-q-v1.json](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/test/resources/dao/space/datomic-q-v1.json), [datomic-q-v1.provenance.edn](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/test/resources/dao/space/datomic-q-v1.provenance.edn#L9-L13), [datomic-q-v1.README.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/test/resources/dao/space/datomic-q-v1.README.md#L129-L130), and [`resource-blake3`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/test/dao/space/datomic_query_conformance_test.cljc#L95-L100) (`51e021815d94ea0f9e4a9af119590c19af2a7450b20db7c7e918c0a0c7bb128c`). All 14 `rules.*` cases and `agg.non-variable-argument` honestly record `\\\"evidence\\\": \\\"local-dao-source\\\"` and `\\\"oracle\\\": \\\"pending\\\"`.\\n- **Phase 2 carries resolved cleanly**:\\n  - [`cell-same?`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/test/dao/space/datomic_query_conformance_test.cljc#L322-L332) now enforces a consuming one-to-one matching (exact because numeric-value equality `(zero? (cbor/num-compare a b))` is an equivalence relation on numerics).\\n  - [`parse-aggregate`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2374-L2376) (backed by [`check-declared-symbols`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2477-L2481) for bare/`_` symbols) refuses non-variable aggregate arguments statically, and [`validate-clauses!`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2192-L2194) + [`clause-bound-vars`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2501) refuse non-flat rule calls cleanly.\\n  - E15 ([datomic-q-v1.errata.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/test/resources/dao/space/datomic-q-v1.errata.md#L242-L251)) accurately records the two-layer `rand`/`sample` refusal, `(max n ?x)` tie order, and the non-variable aggregate-arg refusal.\\n- **Inaccuracy in E16 (D4)**: E16 ([datomic-q-v1.errata.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/test/resources/dao/space/datomic-q-v1.errata.md#L117-L119)) claims unbound required-bound rule calls surface through the adapter as `:evaluation-failed`, when in fact both [`classify-core-failure`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query/datomic.cljc#L579-L583) and [`the-adapter-classifies-rule-refusals`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/test/dao/space/query_rules_test.cljc#L375-L377) classify them as **`:invalid-request`** (`:cognitect.anomalies/incorrect`).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. Defects Missed by the Review Chain\\n\\n1. **P1 | [query.cljc:2066-2083](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2066-L2083) ([`rule-fixpoint`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2057-L2083), [`note-hit`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L1969-L1973), [`clear-hit`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L1976-L1978)) | Concurrent `rule-fixpoint` leader activations for the same `call-key` clobber (and on `reduced`, leak) `(::hits st)`, losing answers on left-recursive multi-call queries (D1)**\\n   - **Evidence / trace**: [`rule-iteration`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2049) invokes `(k st (:acc a2') b')` mid-pass. `k` closes over the caller's `ctx` ([query.cljc:2204-2205](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2204-L2205)), where `call-key` is *not* in `::tables`. On the suite's own `graph` (`1->2->3->1, 3->4, 5->6`) and `left-rules`, consider:\\n     ```clojure\\n     (qq '[:find ?x ?y :in $ % :where (path 1 ?x) (path 1 ?y)] (graph) left-rules)\\n     ```\\n     Both clauses share `call-key = ['path (binding-key [1 FREE])]`. During Pass 1 of outer `(path 1 ?x)`, Def 1 calls [`read-table`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2001) once before `each-st` (setting `::hits = #{K}`), derives `[1 3]` (`?x = 3`), and streams to `k` (`(path 1 ?y)`). Inner `(path 1 ?y)` sees `table = nil` in outer `ctx`, runs its own `rule-fixpoint` for `K`, and exits at [line 2082](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2082) via `:else [(clear-hit st K) acc']` — **erasing `K` from `(::hits st)`**. Outer Pass 1 finishes with `(:new a2) = [[1 3]]` and `(hit? st K) => false`, stopping at Pass 1 and silently losing `?x = 1` and `?x = 4` (returning 8 of 16 rows; with recursive-first definition order, stopping at Pass 0 and losing `?x = 3` as well). The same bug hits `(path ?a ?b) (path ?c ?d)` (`K = ['path [FREE FREE]]`) and `(path 1 ?x) (not-join [?x] (path 1 ?z) ...)`. Conversely, [line 2078](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2078) (`stopped? [st (reduced acc')]`) omits `clear-hit`, leaking an inner `exists-st` hit into `st`.\\n   - **Why existing tests missed it**: [`a-rule-used-twice-in-one-query-is-independent-per-call`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/test/dao/space/query_rules_test.cljc#L163-L166) used `(path 1 ?x) (path 5 ?y)` (distinct keys), and [`execution_test.cljc:426`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/dao/space/query/execution_test.cljc#L426) used right-recursive `chain-rules` (which binds `?m` to distinct keys and never needs Pass 1).\\n   - **Recommended correction**: Capture `was-hit? (hit? st call-key)` on entry to [`rule-fixpoint`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2066) and restore `(if was-hit? (note-hit st call-key) (clear-hit st call-key))` on both `stopped?` ([line 2078](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2078)) and `:else` ([line 2082](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2082)), leaving `(exec/terminal? st)` untouched (or allocate a unique table-activation ID in `st`). Pin same-key sibling calls `(path 1 ?x) (path 1 ?y)` with `left-rules` (both clause orders) and `(path 1 ?x) (not-join [?x] (path 1 ?z) ...)` in [query_rules_test.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/test/dao/space/query_rules_test.cljc).\\n\\n2. **P2 (Gate Blocker) | [jolt_j2_lane.clj:253-274](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj#L253-L274) | `dao.space.query-rules-test` is unlisted in the Jolt J2 manifest (D2)**\\n   - **Evidence**: Branch `datomic-q-p3-ci` adds portable [query_rules_test.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/test/dao/space/query_rules_test.cljc) without adding `\\\"dao.space.query-rules-test\\\"` to `included` in [jolt_j2_lane.clj](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj). Merging as-is will break [`check-manifest!`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj#L327-L363) on `master` (`J2 manifest FAILED: UNLISTED dao.space.query-rules-test`, sixth recurrence) and omit a pure query suite required by [dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md:924-925](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/docs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md#L924-L925).\\n   - **Recommended correction**: Add `\\\"dao.space.query-rules-test\\\"` to `included` in [jolt_j2_lane.clj](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj#L256) and run the Jolt single-namespace check before merge.\\n\\n3. **P2 | [query.cljc:1958-1966, 2093, 2552](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L1958-L1966) | Non-sequential rule heads bypass `check-rules-stratified!` or misclassify as `:evaluation-failed` (D3)**\\n   - **Evidence**: [`check-rules-stratified!`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2552) filters by `(sequential? (first %))`, whereas [`emit-rule`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2093) uses `(first (first %))` and [`rule-head`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L1959) uses `(vec (rest head))`. A set head `'[[#{p} [1 :e 2] (not (p))]]` skips `check-rules-stratified!` (`(sequential? #{p}) => false`) yet evaluates in `emit-rule`/`rule-head` without refusal; a scalar head `'[[123 [1 :e 2]]]` throws raw host `IllegalArgumentException` in `(first (first %))`, surfacing at the adapter as `:evaluation-failed` (`fault`) instead of `:invalid-request` (`incorrect`).\\n   - **Recommended correction**: Require `(and (sequential? rule) (sequential? (first rule)) (symbol? (ffirst rule)))` in rule validation / [`rule-head`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L1958) (throwing `ex-info` `\\\"malformed rule head\\\"` with `{:head ...}`) so stratification, core evaluation, and adapter `:invalid-request` classification share one exact head grammar.\\n\\n4. **P2 | [datomic-q-v1.errata.md:117-119](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/test/resources/dao/space/datomic-q-v1.errata.md#L117-L119) | E16 misstates the adapter error discriminator for unbound required-bound rule calls (D4)**\\n   - **Evidence**: Core throws `(ex-info \\\"Rule required-bound variable is not bound at the call\\\" {:rule rule-name, :var ...})` ([query.cljc:2026-2027](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2026-L2027)). Because `(some? (ex-data e))` is true, [`classify-core-failure`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query/datomic.cljc#L579-L583) maps it to **`:invalid-request`** (`:cognitect.anomalies/incorrect`), pinned at [query_rules_test.cljc:375-377](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/test/dao/space/query_rules_test.cljc#L375-L377) — not `:evaluation-failed` (`:cognitect.anomalies/fault`).\\n   - **Recommended correction**: Update E16 to name `:invalid-request` (`:cognitect.anomalies/incorrect`, via the adapter's generic core-`ex-info` refusal path, consistent with unbound fn/`not-join` variables), keeping Datomic's exact category on the Phase 5 oracle measurement list.\\n\\n5. **P3 | [dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md:233](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/docs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md#L233) | Stale `active-call guard` text in adjacent supported-domain row (D5)**\\n   - **Recommended correction**: While editing the branch for D1–D4, update row 233 (`Finite positive recursive rules`) alongside row 232 so it no longer states `\\\"Current active-call guard is not a completeness proof\\\"`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. Sign-Off Verdict\\n\\nNOT SIGNED OFF: Fix D1 (`rule-fixpoint` `::hits` preservation across nested same-`call-key` leader activations on both normal and `reduced` exits, with left-recursive same-key conjunction/negation regression tests), D2 (register `\\\"dao.space.query-rules-test\\\"` in `src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj` and verify on Jolt), D3 (reject non-sequential/malformed rule heads uniformly with `ex-info` so stratification cannot be bypassed by set heads and adapter errors stay `:invalid-request`), and D4 (correct `:evaluation-failed` to `:invalid-request` in `datomic-q-v1.errata.md` E16; optionally fold D5 on `dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md:233`), then re-verify and return for confirmation and sign-off.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ncollab/1792962000000-architect-datomic-q-phase3-resignoff.gpt-6-astra.stdout.log:12:{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_5\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'git diff 164da9c0..5dbe4c5f; git worktree list'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\ncollab/1792962000000-architect-datomic-q-phase3-resignoff.gpt-6-astra.stdout.log:13:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_5\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'git diff 164da9c0..5dbe4c5f; git worktree list'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"diff --git a/docs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md b/docs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md\\nindex f126359c..e5dec103 100644\\n--- a/docs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md\\n+++ b/docs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md\\n@@ -230,7 +230,7 @@ domain. It does not mean oracle verification has already occurred.\\n | Multiple sources and input binding forms | Exact target | Core presence verified; differential fixtures required. |\\n | Negation/disjunction | Exact target for declared supported forms | Binding, scope and error behavior require conformance. |\\n | Required-bound rule heads | Implemented (Phase 3) | `(r [?x] ?y)` heads with flat calls `(r 1 ?y)`; an unbound required argument fails at the call. |\\n-| Finite positive recursive rules | Exact target after conformance | Current active-call guard is not a completeness proof. Work budget provides an execution backstop. |\\n+| Finite positive recursive rules | Exact target after conformance | Implemented (Phase 3): per-call-key tabling with an immutable least fixed point (replaces the active-call guard); recursion through negation is refused before evaluation; the exact rule-head grammar is `[(name args...) body...]`. Work budget provides the execution backstop for fresh-value recursion. |\\n | Numeric identity/arithmetic | Documented difference | Preserve the ratified CBOR identity policy and explicit unsupported-carrier refusals. |\\n | `get-else`, `missing?` | Exact target on supported fact sources | Already index-aware special forms; edge semantics pending oracle cases. |\\n | Deterministic aggregates | Exact target within declared numeric domain | Existing six plus additions specified below; edge cases pending. |\\ndiff --git a/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc b/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc\\nindex 75e5bca9..4c46c49d 100644\\n--- a/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc\\n+++ b/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc\\n@@ -2064,7 +2064,12 @@\\n    pass finds nothing new; the work budget is the backstop when fresh values\\n    keep generating new tuples. A pass's progress is the state it returns.\\\"\\n   [st ctx binding rule-name call-args arg-vals call-key defs acc k]\\n-  (let [run (fn run [st table acc]\\n+  (let [;; a nested leader of the SAME key (k runs mid-pass) must hand the\\n+        ;; outer leader's marker back on exit, not erase or leak its own\\n+        was-hit? (hit? st call-key)\\n+        restore (fn [st]\\n+                  (if was-hit? (note-hit st call-key) (clear-hit st call-key)))\\n+        run (fn run [st table acc]\\n               (let [st (clear-hit st call-key)\\n                     a2 {:seen (:seen table), :new [], :acc acc}]\\n                 (bind (bounce (fn []\\n@@ -2075,11 +2080,11 @@\\n                               a2 (unreduced a2)\\n                               acc' (:acc a2)]\\n                           (cond\\n-                            stopped? [st (reduced acc')]\\n+                            stopped? [(restore st) (reduced acc')]\\n                             (exec/terminal? st) [st acc']\\n                             (and (seq (:new a2)) (hit? st call-key))\\n                             (run st {:tuples (into (:tuples table) (:new a2)), :seen (:seen a2)} acc')\\n-                            :else [(clear-hit st call-key) acc']))))))]\\n+                            :else [(restore st) acc']))))))]\\n     (run st {:tuples [], :seen #{}} acc)))\\n \\n \\n@@ -2549,7 +2554,14 @@\\n    negation inside a cycle has no such meaning here and is refused.\\\"\\n   [rules]\\n   (when (sequential? rules)\\n-    (let [named (filter #(and (sequential? %) (sequential? (first %))) rules)\\n+    (doseq [rule rules]\\n+      (when-not (and (sequential? rule)\\n+                     (sequential? (first rule))\\n+                     (symbol? (ffirst rule)))\\n+        (throw (ex-info \\\"malformed rule head: a rule is [(name args...) body...]\\\"\\n+                        {:head (when (sequential? rule) (first rule))\\n+                         :rule rule}))))\\n+    (let [named rules\\n           calls (reduce (fn [m rule]\\n                           (update m (first (first rule)) (fnil into [])\\n                                   (collect-rule-calls (rest rule) false)))\\ndiff --git a/src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj b/src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj\\nindex ccef2f2a..0249409b 100644\\n--- a/src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj\\n+++ b/src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj\\n@@ -254,6 +254,8 @@\\n    ;; Listed 2026-10-26 (Phase 2 merge note, argon sign-off condition):\\n    ;; the portable aggregate/E3/E13 suite — pure logic, no sockets/fs.\\n    \\\"dao.space.query-aggregates-test\\\"\\n+   ;; Listed 2026-10-26 (Phase 3): portable rules/recursion suite, pure logic.\\n+   \\\"dao.space.query-rules-test\\\"\\n    \\\"dao.space.stigmergy-test\\\" ; rejoined (J4a)\\n    \\\"dao.space.store.fs-test\\\" ; rejoined (J4b)\\n    ;; Listed 2026-10-25: added by 3d77ed52 without a manifest entry, which\\ndiff --git a/test/dao/space/query_rules_test.cljc b/test/dao/space/query_rules_test.cljc\\nindex fbb9c1f0..38b6534e 100644\\n--- a/test/dao/space/query_rules_test.cljc\\n+++ b/test/dao/space/query_rules_test.cljc\\n@@ -378,3 +378,48 @@\\n   (let [d (adapter-error (fn [] (dq/q '[:find ?e :in $ % :where (fan [2] ?e)]\\n                                 (friends) '[[(fan [?x] ?e) [?e :f ?x]]])))]\\n     (is (= :invalid-request (::dq/error d)))))\\n+\\n+\\n+;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n+;; Same-key nested leaders and the exact head grammar (phase 3 audit D1, D3)\\n+;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n+\\n+(def ^:private reach-1 #{1 2 3 4})\\n+\\n+\\n+(deftest same-call-key-siblings-keep-every-row\\n+  (let [full (set (for [x reach-1 y reach-1] [x y]))]\\n+    (testing \\\"both clause orders, left recursion\\\"\\n+      (is (= full (qq '[:find ?x ?y :in $ % :where (path 1 ?x) (path 1 ?y)]\\n+                      (graph) left-rules)))\\n+      (is (= full (qq '[:find ?x ?y :in $ % :where (path 1 ?y) (path 1 ?x)]\\n+                      (graph) left-rules))))\\n+    (testing \\\"the other recursion shapes agree\\\"\\n+      (doseq [rules [right-rules both-rules]]\\n+        (is (= full (qq '[:find ?x ?y :in $ % :where (path 1 ?x) (path 1 ?y)]\\n+                        (graph) rules)))))\\n+    (testing \\\"an inner existential over the same key does not leak or erase\\\"\\n+      (is (= (set (map vector reach-1))\\n+             (qq '[:find ?x :in $ % :where (path 1 ?x)\\n+                   (not-join [?x] (path 1 ?z) [(= ?z 99)])]\\n+                 (graph) left-rules)))\\n+      (is (= #{} (qq '[:find ?x :in $ % :where (path 1 ?x)\\n+                       (not-join [?x] (path 1 ?z) [(= ?z ?z)])]\\n+                     (graph) left-rules)))\\n+      (is (= full (qq '[:find ?x ?y :in $ % :where (path 1 ?x)\\n+                        (not-join [] (path 1 ?z) [(= ?z 99)]) (path 1 ?y)]\\n+                      (graph) left-rules))))))\\n+\\n+\\n+(deftest malformed-rule-heads-are-refused-uniformly\\n+  (doseq [[label rules] {\\\"set head\\\" '[[#{p ?x} [?x :e _]]]\\n+                         \\\"scalar head\\\" '[[p [?x :e _]]]\\n+                         \\\"non-symbol name\\\" '[[(1 ?x) [?x :e _]]]\\n+                         \\\"non-sequential rule\\\" '[#{(p ?x)}]}]\\n+    (testing label\\n+      (is (refused-with? (fn [] (qq '[:find ?x :in $ % :where (p ?x)] (graph) rules))\\n+                         #\\\"malformed rule head\\\")\\n+          (str \\\"core: \\\" label))\\n+      (let [d (adapter-error (fn [] (dq/q '[:find ?x :in $ % :where (p ?x)]\\n+                                        (graph) rules)))]\\n+        (is (= :invalid-request (::dq/error d)) (str \\\"adapter: \\\" label))))))\\ndiff --git a/test/resources/dao/space/datomic-q-v1.errata.md b/test/resources/dao/space/datomic-q-v1.errata.md\\nindex 8921f7d2..c1093cf2 100644\\n--- a/test/resources/dao/space/datomic-q-v1.errata.md\\n+++ b/test/resources/dao/space/datomic-q-v1.errata.md\\n@@ -178,10 +178,14 @@ behavior is unmeasured):\\n   `(r 2 3 ?z)`. A required position that is unbound at the call (a variable\\n   with no binding, or `_`) throws \\\"Rule required-bound variable is not\\n   bound at the call\\\" naming the variable, evaluated with the bindings at the\\n-  call (a later clause does not rescue it). Through the adapter this surfaces\\n-  as the generic `:evaluation-failed` path, deliberately: the error is\\n-  binding-dependent and not statically decidable. It joins the Phase 5 oracle\\n-  measurement list. A vector inside a call is\\n+  call (a later clause does not rescue it). The error carries ex-data, so\\n+  through the adapter `classify-core-failure` maps it to\\n+  `:invalid-request` / `:incorrect` (pinned in `query_rules_test`), not\\n+  `:evaluation-failed`; it is raised at evaluation, not statically, because\\n+  it is binding-dependent. Datomic's exact category stays on the Phase 5\\n+  oracle measurement list. A rule that is not `[(name args...) body...]`\\n+  (set or scalar head, non-symbol name) is refused \\\"malformed rule head\\\"\\n+  before stratification and evaluation, `:invalid-request` at the adapter. A vector inside a call is\\n   refused (\\\"rule call arguments are flat\\\"); a vector anywhere but the head's\\n   leading position is a malformed head. Datomic's own diagnostics are\\n   unmeasured.\\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld                                     671cd21f [master]\\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-ble                                 57207b36 [ble-track]\\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-codec-c2-old                        47f43405 (detached HEAD)\\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-php-p3b                             b2366971 [yang-php-p3b]\\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-ts-t2b                              034efe9e [yang-ts-t2b]\\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes  5dbe4c5f [datomic-q-p3-ci]\\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0b          6fa97400 [jolt-j0b]\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ncollab/1792962000000-architect-datomic-q-phase3-resignoff.gpt-6-astra.stdout.log:14:{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_6\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat docs/agents/roles/architect.md .agents/skills/code-review-pr/references/review_checklist.md; python3 .agents/skills/code-review-pr/scripts/pr_reviewer.py analyze --target 164da9c0..5dbe4c5f'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\ncollab/1792962000000-architect-datomic-q-phase3-resignoff.gpt-6-astra.stdout.log:15:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_6\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat docs/agents/roles/architect.md .agents/skills/code-review-pr/references/review_checklist.md; python3 .agents/skills/code-review-pr/scripts/pr_reviewer.py analyze --target 164da9c0..5dbe4c5f'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"---\\ndescription: Lead System Architect role definition for datom.world\\n---\\n\\n# ROLE: Lead System Architect\\n\\n## Domain Scope\\n\\n- Foundational axioms, architectural invariants, and design contracts\\n- Subsystem boundaries, interpreters, host isolation, and explicit causality\\n- Cross-platform architecture, migration strategy, and compatibility boundaries\\n- ADR coherence, domain vocabulary, and theoretical grounding where useful\\n- Architecture review for high-risk or cross-cutting changes\\n- Commit sign-off: the sign-off on completed, review-reconciled work that\\n  authorizes the orchestrator to stage, commit, merge, and push it\\n  (trivial direct edits are exempt; see\\n  [`orchestrator.md`](orchestrator.md#coordination-contract))\\n\\nThis role owns no permanent file list. Each task defines the artifacts it may\\ninspect or change and any permitted expansion.\\n\\n## Core Responsibilities\\n\\n1. **Protect Invariants**: Strictly enforce the 6 non-negotiable invariants (no hidden global state, no implicit control flow, no raw callbacks, no shared mutable state, no layer collapsing, no assumed graphs).\\n2. **Decompose Complexity**: When new requirements emerge, decompose them into append-only streams, explicit interpreters, and immutable datom representations.\\n3. **Malleability Governance**: Ensure architecture adheres to bounded complexity, loose coupling, and high cohesion as defined in [`docs/agents/malleability.md`](../malleability.md).\\n4. **Lineage Alignment**: Keep designs grounded in Plan 9 / Datomic / Lisp architectural lineage.\\n\\n## Delegation Prompt Template\\n\\n```text\\nCreated-GMT: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS GMT>\\nCreated-Local: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS local-timezone-name>\\n\\n# Task: <Task Name>\\n\\nRole: Lead System Architect\\n\\nImplementers:\\n- Model: <model-name> | Assigned: <local timestamp> | Status: active | Rationale: <why>\\n\\nPerform a read-only architecture review of <design-change>.\\n\\nRead first:\\n- docs/design/datom.world.md\\n- <target-design-file>\\n- <relevant-implementation-boundary>\\n- <relevant-contract-tests>\\n\\nEvaluate foundational invariants, ownership boundaries, explicit state and\\ncontrol flow, concurrency and linearization, dynamic extension, host isolation,\\nCLJ/CLJS/CLJD portability, migration risk, completion criteria, and design\\ncontradictions. Distinguish architectural defects from implementation gaps or\\nintentionally deferred work. Do not edit files.\\n\\nBegin the final response exactly with:\\nCompleted-GMT: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS GMT>\\nCompleted-Local: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS local-timezone-name>\\n\\nThen report: severity | file:line | invariant/evidence | recommended correction.\\nAlso confirm the requested properties that passed review.\\n```\\n# Code Review PR Checklist & Taxonomy\\n\\nWhen performing code reviews, evaluate changes using this structured checklist and severity taxonomy.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Finding Severity Taxonomy\\n\\n| Severity | Label | Definition | Examples |\\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\\n| **P0** | **Critical (Blocker)** | Security vulnerabilities, data loss risks, production crashes, secret leakage. Must be fixed before merging. | Hardcoded tokens, unhandled NullPointer on critical path, SQL injection, broken auth check. |\\n| **P1** | **High (Must Address)** | Logic bugs, breaking API changes, missing error handling on external calls, race conditions, lack of tests for complex logic. | Swallowed exceptions, broken retry loop, missing backward compatibility in API schema. |\\n| **P2** | **Medium (Recommended)** | Performance inefficiencies, code duplication, sub-optimal data structures, non-idiomatic style. | Unnecessary DB query inside loop, missing index, missing parameter validation. |\\n| **P3** | **Low (Nit / Suggestion)** | Minor formatting, naming improvements, leftover comments/TODOs, minor doc polish. | Variable naming clarity, typos in docstrings, cleaning leftover TODO comments. |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Comprehensive Review Checklist\\n\\n### A. Logic & Correctness\\n- [ ] **Edge Cases**: Does the code handle null/nil/undefined, empty collections, zero values, boundary numbers, and unexpected inputs?\\n- [ ] **State & Concurrency**: Are shared state mutations thread-safe? Are locks acquired/released properly without deadlock risks?\\n- [ ] **Control Flow**: Are all conditional branches covered? Do loops have guaranteed termination conditions?\\n- [ ] **Error Propagation**: Are errors caught and logged/surfaced appropriately, rather than swallowed silently (`catch (Exception e) {}`)?\\n\\n### B. Security & Credentials\\n- [ ] **No Hardcoded Secrets**: Are API keys, passwords, bearer tokens, or private keys excluded from code and config?\\n- [ ] **Input Validation & Sanitization**: Are external inputs validated before processing or passing to system shells, DB queries, or HTML rendering?\\n- [ ] **Authentication & Authorization**: Do endpoints verify user identity and check permissions before executing state changes?\\n- [ ] **Safe Dependencies**: Are newly added packages pinned to trusted versions without known vulnerabilities?\\n\\n### C. Architecture & API Design\\n- [ ] **Preserve API Contracts**: Are public method signatures, REST endpoints, and schema definitions backward compatible?\\n- [ ] **Single Responsibility**: Are modules, classes, and functions focused on a clear, single responsibility?\\n- [ ] **Coupling & Cohesion**: Is the new code properly modularized without introducing circular dependencies or leaky abstractions?\\n- [ ] **Idempotence**: Are retry loops or state-changing operations safe to re-execute on transient failures?\\n\\n### D. Performance & Resource Efficiency\\n- [ ] **N+1 Queries**: Are database or remote API calls executed in batches rather than inside loops?\\n- [ ] **Resource Cleanup**: Are file handles, database connections, streams, and web sockets closed explicitly (or managed via try-with-resources / context managers)?\\n- [ ] **Memory & Allocation**: Are large datasets streamed or paginated rather than loaded fully into memory at once?\\n\\n### E. Test Coverage & Quality\\n- [ ] **Test Coverage**: Do new features or bug fixes include corresponding unit or integration tests?\\n- [ ] **Test Quality**: Do tests verify actual assertions rather than just checking that code runs without throwing?\\n- [ ] **Edge Case Tests**: Are failure modes, invalid inputs, and error handlers covered by unit tests?\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. Review Feedback Guidelines\\n\\n1. **Be Specific**: Always reference the exact file line number, function name, and context.\\n2. **Explain the \\\"Why\\\"**: Don't just say \\\"change this\\\". Explain the risk or benefit (e.g., \\\"This could lead to a race condition if two threads call `transact!` simultaneously...\\\").\\n3. **Provide Concrete Fixes**: Offer concrete, copy-pasteable diff snippets where appropriate.\\n4. **Acknowledge Good Work**: Highlight well-crafted solutions, thorough tests, or clean refactorings.\\n# Code Review Summary for `164da9c0..5dbe4c5f`\\n\\n## Executive Overview\\n- **Total Files Changed:** 5\\n- **Lines Added:** +72 | **Lines Deleted:** -9\\n- **Test-to-Source Additions Ratio:** 2.94 (53 test lines vs 18 source lines)\\n- **Overall Change Risk:** `LOW`\\n\\n### Included Commits\\n- 5dbe4c5f fix(dao.space.query): same-key nested leader hit marker, exact rule-head grammar, lane manifest, E16 category\\n\\n## Automated Scan Findings\\n✅ No critical security or code quality smells detected by automated scan.\\n\\n## File Churn & Risk Breakdown\\n| File Path | Category | +Add | -Del | Risk |\\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\\n| `src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc` | Source Code | +16 | -4 | `Medium` |\\n| `src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj` | Source Code | +2 | -0 | `Medium` |\\n| `test/dao/space/query_rules_test.cljc` | Tests | +45 | -0 | `Low` |\\n| `test/resources/dao/space/datomic-q-v1.errata.md` | Tests | +8 | -4 | `Low` |\\n| `docs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md` | Documentation | +1 | -1 | `Low` |\\n\\n## Reviewer Focus & Recommendations\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ncollab/1792962000000-architect-datomic-q-phase3-resignoff.gpt-6-astra.stdout.log:19:{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_9\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"cat docs/agents/build-n-test.md; sed -n '1,150p' deps.edn; sed -n '1,100p' src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj; rg -n 'jolt|5dbe|78 assertions' collab/1792962000000*fix* collab/1792962000000*resign*\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
